array2: asubsref(bin,0) ... asubsref(bin,n-1)
array3: asubsref(w,0) ... asubsref(w,n-1) If this assumption is correct and asubsref does not produce any side effects, the following invariant can be derived: After the end of the execution of the loop, array2[j] is incremented
  by the number x which is the largest number such that sum of array3[i]
  for i from 0 to x is smaller than array1[j]. Here is what you can do. First, you can merge the two innermost loops since ( under our assumption ) their iterations are independent: for(i=0; i<n; i++)
