Why the 16 Threads case differs so much from the others? I'm running
the algorithm on a Google VM machine with 24 Threads and 96 GB of ram. As you have mentioned on the comments: It's a Intel Xeon CPU @2.30 GHz, 12 physical core That is the reason that when you moved to 16 thread you stop (almost) linearly scaling, because you are no longer just using physical cores but also logic cores ( i.e., hyper-threading). I expected that static would be the best since the iterations takes
