You are adding the time used by each thread to tot_time and comparing that to the time when only one thread is used. Doing this tot_time for all threads will in most cases ( exception for super linear speedups ) be greater or equal to the time for when only one thread is used. The ideal case is when they are equal that means the time was evenly distributed across all threads. So your definition of tot_time is an interesting metric to test how well the load is distributed but I don't think it is what you are looking for. Instead you could report the time of the thread that took the maximum time. But only reporting the time used inside the parallel region removes the cost of the overhead of implementing the work sharing by OpenMP.  Instead I would report the time used by the entire work sharing region as in the following code. #include <stdlib.h>
