Total time taken by all the threads = 0.53 seconds Your operation is memory bandwidth bound so I don't see much benefit after two threads on my dual channel DDR4 system. With NUMA systems memory locality can have a big effect.  Since the pages are only allocated the first time they are touched then for benchmarking it may make sense to write to the arrays in parallel first.  The following code will do this but it only works for static scheduling. Make sure to disable dynamic adjustment of the number of threads (not to be confused with dynamic scheduling) with e.g. export OMP_DYNAMIC=false . #include <stdlib.h>
